{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they took the soot of the furnace.</b> Their handfuls, as stated, and Moses threw all. It is possible that the magicians were not struck by the plague of frogs and the mixed swarms, because by their wisdom they sought a way through the wisdom of outcomes to gain a little for themselves, and now their wisdom was extinguished; therefore he mentioned this. And because the plague did not last long, Pharaoh did not ask them to intercede. And because the first plague lasted seven days, we do not learn from it by way of peshat that every plague lasted likewise — rather, we pursue what is after the verse. And it is known that the plague of pestilence was a single hour, and the plague of darkness three days; therefore there is no way for us to know in which month Moses came and the plagues began, except if there is a tradition in the hands of our holy sages — we accept and we hear."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אחר הכתוב נרדוף' is rendered hyper-literally as 'we pursue what is after the verse'; the idiom means to follow the plain sequence of the text, but the rendering preserves the compressed Hebrew construction."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:56.433111509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}